#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# mantissa_exponent

#% text
# `mantissa_exponent(x)` gives `[m, e]` with `x = m 10^e` and `1/10 <= |m| < 1`; `mantissa_exponent(x, b)` does the same in base `b`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact numbers give exact mantissas; zero gives `[0, 0]`; lists thread.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mantissa_exponent(3.4*10^30)
#% output
#= [0.34, 31]

#% cell
mantissa_exponent(123451)
#% output
#= [123451/1000000, 6]

#% cell
mantissa_exponent(1027, 2)
#% output
#= [1027/2048, 11]

#% cell
mantissa_exponent(exp(pi), 2)
#% output
#= [(1/32)*exp(pi), 5]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integer_length`, `real_digits`
